From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0948 redfin: display-engine dump and scanout test pokes (p mdp
 dump|smmu|test|scale|restore)

Steps (a)-(c) of docs/redfin/scanout-plan.md, inert unless poked:
p mdp dump logs the MDP blocks ABL set up (top, CTL0-3, VIG0/1 with their
QSEED3LITE scalers, DMA0-2, LM0/1, PP0/1, DSC0/1, INTF1); p mdp smmu [walk]
reads the apps SMMU match registers and context bank for the MDP streams
(0xb40/0x402); p mdp test points VIG0/VIG1 at a test pattern at 0xa1400000
in the splash region; p mdp scale shows a 1125x2436 pattern (4608-byte rows)
through both scalers (bilinear, overlapping 563-column crops, right pipe at
phase 0.5). Both save every pipe register first, stop presents and 0905's
flips, and put everything back after SECS (default 10) or at p mdp restore.

---
